# Privacy Policy

## Who we are

[COMPANY NAME] ([ADDRESS]) is the controller of the personal data described in
this notice.

If you have any questions, contact us at [EMAIL].

## The short version

- Your creatures are stored in **your own iCloud account**. We cannot see them.
- We only hold data about creatures you choose to **share** with other users.
- We do not use any analytics or tracking of our own.
- We never sell your data and we do not use it for advertising.
- Files you export contain no information about you.

## What we collect and why

### Creatures you keep to yourself

Creatures in your own collection are stored in your personal iCloud account
using Apple's CloudKit service. They are held under your Apple Account, not
ours, and we have no access to them. Apple's handling of that data is covered by
[Apple's privacy policy](https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/).

If you use the app without signing in to iCloud, your creatures stay on your
device and we hold nothing.

### Creatures you share

When you choose to share a creature, it is copied to a shared area of our
CloudKit database so other users can find and breed with it. That record
contains:

- the creature's genetic data and appearance
- its lineage — which creatures it descends from
- the name you gave it
- an anonymous account identifier generated by Apple

The identifier is created by Apple, is specific to this app, and cannot be used
to identify you by name. We do not display it, and nothing in the app shows
other users who created a creature.

**Why:** to provide the sharing and breeding features you have asked to use.
**Lawful basis:** performance of our contract with you.

### Purchases

If you buy the [UNLOCK NAME], the purchase is handled entirely by Apple through
the App Store. We do not see or store your payment details, your name, or your
billing address. We receive only confirmation from Apple that the purchase
applies to your account.

### Support

If you contact us for help, we keep your message and our reply.

**Why:** to answer you and to keep a record of the issue.
**Lawful basis:** our legitimate interest in providing support.

### Reports about content

If you report a creature or a creature name, we keep the report and what we did
about it.

**Why:** to keep the app safe and to act on repeated problems.
**Lawful basis:** our legitimate interest in maintaining a safe service.

### Analytics

We do not use any analytics or crash reporting service of our own, and the app
contains no third-party tracking software.

Apple provides us with anonymous, aggregated statistics about App Store
downloads and app usage through App Store Connect. This information comes from
Apple, is not linked to individual users, and is only available to us if you
have agreed to share analytics with developers in your device settings. You can
change that at any time in **Settings → Privacy & Security → Analytics &
Improvements**.

We do not use your data for advertising, we do not allow anyone else to do so,
and we do not track you across other apps or websites.

## Your camera

The app uses your camera for augmented reality features, so you can see your
creatures in the space around you. Camera images are processed entirely on your
device. They are not sent to us and we do not store them.

Any photo or video you capture is saved by you, to your own device, and we do
not receive a copy.

You can refuse or withdraw camera access at any time in your device settings.
The rest of the app works without it.

## Who we share data with

We do not sell your personal data.

We share it only with:

- **Apple**, which provides the iCloud storage and payment processing the app
  depends on
- **Other users**, who can see creatures you have chosen to share, including the
  name you gave them. They cannot see who created a creature.

We may also disclose information where the law requires it.

## Where your data goes

Data stored through CloudKit is held by Apple in [REGION]. Apple's arrangements
for international transfers are described in its privacy policy.

## How long we keep it

| Data | Kept for |
| --- | --- |
| Creatures in your own collection | Until you delete them. Held in your iCloud account, not ours |
| Shared creatures | Until you remove them from sharing. Creatures other users have already bred from them remain in their collections |
| Purchase records | 7 years, for tax and accounting purposes |
| Support messages | 2 years |
| Content reports | 2 years |

## Your rights

You have the right to:

- ask what personal data we hold about you and get a copy
- have inaccurate data corrected
- have your data deleted
- object to or restrict how we use it
- receive your data in a portable format
- complain to a supervisory authority — in the UK, the Information
  Commissioner's Office at [ico.org.uk](https://ico.org.uk)

To exercise any of these, contact us at [EMAIL]. We will respond within one
month.

**One limitation to be aware of.** If you delete a creature you have shared,
creatures that other users have already bred from it will remain in their
collections. This is unavoidable: those creatures belong to those users, and
their lineage cannot be unwound without deleting other people's work. Any
anonymous identifier linking that shared creature to you can be removed on
request.

## Children

The app is intended to be used by families, and the account holder must be an
adult.

We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under [13/16]. If you
believe a child has provided us with personal data, contact us at [EMAIL] and we
will delete it.

The app does not use behavioural advertising, and does not include any feature
that would let a child be contacted by another user.

## Changes to this notice

If we make significant changes we will tell you in the app before they take
effect.

